1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:09,275
ダイ、接点、基板、冷却が所定環境で長く協調する必要があります。
Survey the complete package: dies, joints, substrate and cooling must cooperate in a specified environment over time.

2
00:00:09,275 --> 00:00:16,650
今日は熱の出口、欠陥の発見、寿命の根拠をたどります。
Today’s route asks whether heat can escape, defects can be found and lifetime claims have evidence.

3
00:00:16,650 --> 00:00:30,000
これらは最終検査だけの問題ではなく、設計の最初から考える問いです。
These questions belong at the beginning of design, not only at final inspection.

4
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:35,381
各ダイで負荷ごとの電力分布を考えます。
Visit each die and consider power distribution under different workloads.

5
00:00:35,381 --> 00:00:41,608
総電力が同じでも熱点の位置で温度は変わります。
Equal total power can produce different temperatures when hotspots move.

6
00:00:41,608 --> 00:01:00,000
冷却設計には場所と時間の情報が必要で、一つの平均電力だけでは全使用条件を表せません。
Cooling design needs spatial and time-dependent information; one average power number cannot represent every operating condition.

7
00:01:00,000 --> 00:01:05,945
ダイから界面材料、ふた、冷却器へ上がります。
Travel upward from the die through interface material, lid and cooler.

8
00:01:05,945 --> 00:01:12,804
厚さ、接触状態、材料特性が熱流を制限します。
Thickness, contact quality and material properties can each restrict heat flow.

9
00:01:12,804 --> 00:01:18,853
冷却器だけを大型化しても解決しない場合があります。
A larger cooler alone may not solve the problem.

10
00:01:18,853 --> 00:01:30,000
部品変更の前に、経路のどこが律速かを探します。
Identify the limiting part of the path before changing the hardware.

11
00:01:30,000 --> 00:01:37,661
ふたと界面を分け、均一な接触と材料の連続性を見ます。
Separate lid and interface to examine uniform contact and material continuity.

12
00:01:37,661 --> 00:01:45,077
厚さの差や空隙は熱抵抗を変え、固定方法も影響します。
Thickness variation and voids can change thermal resistance, while mechanical attachment affects contact.

13
00:01:45,077 --> 00:02:00,000
これは品質を見る枠組みで、実製品へそのまま適用できる圧力や厚さの設定ではありません。
This is an inspection framework, not a transferable prescription for clamping pressure or interface thickness on a real product.

14
00:02:00,000 --> 00:02:06,719
熱は上だけでなく、基板や周囲にも分かれて流れます。
The separated-layer view shows heat can split through the substrate and surrounding structures, not only move upward.

15
00:02:06,719 --> 00:02:13,608
仮定を明示した簡易熱抵抗網は初期検討に役立ちます。
A simplified thermal-resistance network helps early reasoning if its assumptions are stated.

16
00:02:13,608 --> 00:02:30,000
映像の色には温度目盛がなく、接合温度の読み取りや製品合否判定には使えません。
The animation has no temperature scale and cannot provide junction-temperature readings or product acceptance results.

17
00:02:30,000 --> 00:02:39,413
試験信号を追い、部品試験、パッケージ化後の電気試験、システム負荷を区別します。
Follow a test signal and distinguish component tests, post-package electrical tests and system workloads.

18
00:02:39,413 --> 00:02:42,889
検出する故障は異なります。
They expose different failures.

19
00:02:42,889 --> 00:03:00,000
予想外の結果では条件と症状を保存し、電源、配線、熱、論理などへ原因を絞ります。
When a result is unexpected, preserve conditions and symptoms before narrowing the cause to power, interconnect, temperature, logic or another subsystem.

20
00:03:00,000 --> 00:03:08,658
加熱と冷却で異なる材料が接点と界面に繰り返し力を与えます。
Watch conceptual expansion and contraction as different materials load joints and interfaces repeatedly.

21
00:03:08,658 --> 00:03:18,049
信頼性は組立直後の通電だけでなく、時間と繰返しによる変化を扱います。
Reliability concerns change over time and cycling, not merely successful power-on after assembly.

22
00:03:18,049 --> 00:03:30,000
実試験条件は使用環境と適用要件で定め、映像の周期から決めません。
Real test conditions must follow the use environment and applicable qualification requirements, never the timing of this illustration.

23
00:03:30,000 --> 00:03:36,189
画像、電気結果、温度、故障位置を照合します。
Combine images, electrical results, temperatures and failure locations.

24
00:03:36,189 --> 00:03:42,618
一枚の画像は異常を示唆しても根因を証明できません。
One image can suggest a problem without proving its cause.

25
00:03:42,618 --> 00:03:48,216
予測と測定を比べ、誤差と不確かさを記録します。
Compare model predictions with measurements and record error and uncertainty.

26
00:03:48,216 --> 00:04:00,000
見た目のリアルさではなく、検証済みデータで結論を支えます。
Engineering conclusions should be supported by validated data rather than the apparent realism of a visualization.

27
00:04:00,000 --> 00:04:09,578
同じ負荷、環境、測定方法で温度、電力、信頼性、費用を比べます。
Compare package or cooling options under the same workload, environment and measurement method, then evaluate temperature, power, reliability and cost.

28
00:04:09,578 --> 00:04:15,898
多くの条件を同時に変えると、何が効いたか分かりません。
Changing many conditions at once obscures causality.

29
00:04:15,898 --> 00:04:30,000
美しい改善曲線も、再現できる実験へ戻れる必要があります。
An attractive improvement curve must be traceable to an experiment that can be repeated.

30
00:04:30,000 --> 00:04:39,058
要求、熱経路、組立品質、試験、信頼性が循環する全体を見ます。
Rise to see requirements, heat paths, assembly quality, testing and reliability form a feedback loop.

31
00:04:39,058 --> 00:04:47,314
データ、電力、熱に意図した経路があり、結論に根拠があることが美しさです。
Advanced packaging is beautiful when data, power and heat have deliberate routes and conclusions have evidence.

32
00:04:47,314 --> 00:05:00,000
この地図を持って、どのパッケージ技術でもシステム全体の検証を問いましょう。
Carry this map back to any packaging technology and ask how the complete system is verified.
